# OfflineSkins for Fabric 1.21.9-1.21.11
🎨 Display custom skins and capes without relying on Mojang servers.

OfflineSkins allows you to use local player skins and capes on offline-mode servers, private networks, and custom setups.

### The mod is only used when Minecraft cannot retrieve skins from Mojang. It is designed to show on your skin even without an internet connection. However, if your Minecraft client does not have an official license, this mod will show your skin to you, but no one else will see it unless somebody put your skin in their cachedimages folder and also have the mod installed.

### OfflineSkins Reloaded Bug fixes
## What changed?

> Mixins bug fixes
> Rebranding
> Skin and cape servers providers fix

## Providers:
# Before:
```
Shared.downloadSkin(url, Runnable::run)
    .thenApply(Optional::get)
    .thenAccept(data -> {
        if (ImageUtils.validateData(data))
            skin.put(data, ImageUtils.judgeSkinType(data));
    });
```
## Afer:
```
Shared.downloadSkin(url, Runnable::run)
    .thenAccept(optional -> {
        optional.ifPresent(data -> {
            if (ImageUtils.validateData(data)) {
                skin.put(data, ImageUtils.judgeSkinType(data));
            }
        });
    });
```
Note:
1.1.1 is entirly better than 1.1.0 on 1.21.11-1.21.6, but not on 26.1-26.2

## 📁 Simply place your textures into:

> cachedimages/skins/ - Player skins
> 
> cachedimages/capes/ - Player capes

_Exmaple: "cashedimages/skins/steve.png" or "cashedimages/capes/steve.png"_

The file name must match the player's nickname.

✨ Features: • Custom skins from local files • Custom capes support • Works on offline-mode servers • Lightweight and client-side only • No external skin services required

